{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Whirling Rave Lead",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: the huge, whirling, slightly sour lead of early-90s hardcore and rave: detuned pulses churning against each other, each note swooping up into place.\n\nHow it's built: two pulse waves, slightly detuned, their widths swept by one slow LFO (PWM) so they swirl. Each note starts an octave low and glides up: the envelope's INVERTED output, flipped upside down by the Attenuverter (SCALE -1), into both oscillators' FM. Chorus (Ensemble) and Reverb make it enormous.\n\nPlay: chords and slow single notes.\n\nTweak: the swoop envelope's ATTACK (the glide's length), the LFO's RATE, the chorus MODE.",
 "voices": 4,
